# JavaScript YouTube Music provider

GPL-3.0. Catalog renderer parsing was adapted from MetroList's YouTubeItemParser and YouTubeSearchOperations at commit e97197786c2a7ad56279cc9bb4ce3233ef6c99ff. The bootstrap, HTTP bridge, direct stream selection, limited signature interpreter, account authentication and Home integration were written for MetroFuse's public API 1.1.0 and are maintained by 956tris.

The plugin validates the current WEB_REMIX tuple from the service's sw.js_data response. Explicit plugin locale settings override service locale, and Home uses the host's requested locale. The optional host.login ui callback supplies the plugin SDK's WebView screen with plugin-owned navigation rules and labels. SDK browsers capture a candidate session and supply it only through the current activation's bound login callback. The provider verifies an active account before committing it. Credentials never enter ordinary settings or the application's previous YouTube account. The alternate guest ANDROID_VR profile comes from InnerTubeX v0.11.7 at https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/innertubex/tree/v0.11.7.

The MFP has no native executable payload and never evaluates remote player scripts. It supports Home feed, radio and account-library continuations, direct audio and unambiguous signature sequences of reverse, splice and swap. Library exposes the account's songs, albums, artists and playlists using the host's content locale. Liked Music pages, like/unlike/dislike requests and track like status use the same plugin account. Unsupported signature shapes and the throttling n transform produce explicit errors. It does not provide SABR, music video playback, channel switching or saving/removing library collections. Use the native InnerTubeX JAR/APK for full extraction and SABR audio.

All variants use the metrofuse.youtube-music owner. Import one implementation at a time. Build with python tools/package-mfp.py and check the production callbacks with node native/tests/javascript.mjs. The fixtures are synthetic and contain no real account responses or credentials. See the repository README for verification results and remaining manual checks.
